From: FlipperEmu
Subject: [PATCH] hw/sd/ssi-sd: accept a command right after a response

After sending a command response the model stays in SSI_SD_RESPONSE and
consumes one more byte before it is ready for the next command. Hosts that
deselect the card after the response and clock their padding byte with CS
high (the Flipper Zero SD driver, sd_spi_deselect_card_and_purge) lose the
first byte of their next command: CMD8 48 00 00 01 AA 87 was parsed as
CMD0 with argument 0x0001AA87.

Recognise a command start (01xxxxxx) in that state, and in the idle state
ignore bytes that cannot start a command, as a card does.

Signed-off-by: FlipperEmu
---
--- a/hw/sd/ssi-sd.c
+++ b/hw/sd/ssi-sd.c
@@ -146,6 +146,10 @@
             return SSI_DUMMY;
         }
 
+        if ((val & 0xc0) != 0x40) {
+            /* not a command start (start bit 0, transmission bit 1) */
+            return SSI_DUMMY;
+        }
         s->cmd = val & 0x3f;
         s->mode = SSI_SD_CMDARG;
         s->arglen = 0;
@@ -191,6 +195,15 @@
         } else {
             DPRINTF("End of command\n");
             s->mode = SSI_SD_CMD;
+            /*
+             * The card accepts the next command right after its response;
+             * hosts need not clock an extra byte with CS asserted first.
+             */
+            if ((val & 0xc0) == 0x40) {
+                s->cmd = val & 0x3f;
+                s->mode = SSI_SD_CMDARG;
+                s->arglen = 0;
+            }
         }
         return SSI_DUMMY;
     case SSI_SD_PREP_DATA:
